 # NanoApps
 
-The homebrew app framework for the iPod nano 7G: an SDK, a loader that runs inside the
-iPod's own interface, and the source of every app.
-
-This is a fork of [nfzerox/NanoApps](https://github.com/nfzerox/NanoApps). The upstream
-README documents the SDK, the app templates and the full app list; read it there. This copy
-differs in how apps get onto the iPod and stay there:
-
-- **Untethered loading.** Upstream registers apps over USB after every restart. Here a
-  startup loader in `/Apps/Startup` does it at boot (`system/`, `tools/build_ab_resident_loader.py`).
-- **A/B loader slots.** A small selector picks one of two loaders and falls back to the other
-  if it is damaged (`system/resident_selector/`).
-- **Apps load when opened and unload when another opens**, so large apps fit (`system/silver_resident/`).
-- **Ports support**: ARM-state apps with hardware floating point, relocation fixes, and the two
-  game apps `apps/mk64` and `apps/sm64`, which link libraries built from `../games`.
